From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 05:29:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] downloads: keep the process alive in the background on
 HarmonyOS (silent audio + wake lock)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On HarmonyOS 卓易通 the app process is suspended a few seconds after it
leaves the foreground even though the download queue and the library update
run inside WorkManager's dataSync foreground service. Downloads simply stop
until the user reopens Mihon, and since the foreground service itself is
never finished it keeps draining Android 15's 6-hour dataSync budget; when
that runs out the system kills the process with

    ForegroundServiceDidNotStopInTimeException: A foreground service of type
    dataSync did not stop within its timeout

which is exactly what the 2026-10-06 crash log shows. The same behaviour
was verified with Animeko on the same device: dataSync service, partial wake
lock and battery-optimisation exemption are all ignored, only audio output
keeps the container running (animeko-harmony patch 0006).

Add BackgroundKeepAlive: a ref-counted helper that, while at least one job
holds it, loops a silent PCM buffer through an AudioTrack in MODE_STATIC
(written once, looped by the audio HAL, no CPU) and holds a partial wake
lock. No audio focus is requested, so other apps' playback is not ducked or
paused. DownloadWorker and LibraryUpdateWorker acquire it right after
setForeground(); the token is released when the worker's coroutine
completes, fails or is cancelled.

Because the download service now really is playing audio for its whole
lifetime, DownloadWorker declares FOREGROUND_SERVICE_TYPE_MEDIA_PLAYBACK instead
of DATA_SYNC (manifest: dataSync|mediaPlayback + the matching permission).
mediaPlayback has no time limit on Android 15+, so a long queue no longer
hits the 6-hour cut-off. The library update keeps dataSync.

Everything is behind a new switch, Settings → Downloads → "Keep running in
the background (HarmonyOS)", on by default; turning it off restores the
upstream dataSync-only behaviour.

Rebased from the v0.20.4 series (0005): the workers were renamed
DownloadJob -> DownloadWorker and LibraryUpdateJob -> LibraryUpdateWorker
in v0.21.0 and use Metro field injection, so LibraryUpdateWorker gets
DownloadPreferences injected instead of going through Injekt.
